AcquisitionMethod: top 10
AlkylationReagent: iodoacetamide
CleavageAgent: trypsin
CollisionEnergy: 25% normalized collision energy
Disease: pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC)
FlowRateChromatogram: 6 mul/min
FlowRateChromatogram: 300 nl/min
FractionIdentifier: gel band 1
FractionIdentifier: gel band 2
FractionIdentifier: gel band 5
FractionationMethod: protein lysates were separated on pre-cast 4%-12% gradient gels using the NuPAGE SDS-PAGE system (Invitrogen, Carlsbad, CA, USA).
FragmentMassTolerance: 20 ppm
FragmentationMethod: HCD (higher-energy collision)
GradientTime: 10-40% buffer B gradient for 75 min
Instrument: Q Exactive mass spectrometer (Thermo Fisher, Bremen, Germany)
Label: label-free quantification option
MaterialType: tissue
Modification: Cysteine carboxamidomethylation (Cys, +57.021464 Da)
Modification: methionine oxidation (Met, +15.994915 Da)
Modification: N-terminal acetylation (N-terminal, +42.010565 Da)
NumberOfBiologicalReplicates: 3
NumberOfFractions: five bands
NumberOfMissedCleavages: two
NumberOfSamples: 20
Organism: Homo sapiens
OrganismPart: bulk tumor tissue
PrecursorMassTolerance: 4.5 ppm
ReductionReagent: DTT
Separation: Ultimate 3000 nanoLC system (Dionex LC-Packings, Amsterdam, The Netherlands) equipped with a 40 cm x 75 mum internal diameter (ID) fused silica column custom packed with 1.9 mum 120 Aa ReproSil Pur C18 aqua (Dr Maisch GMBH, Ammerbuch-Entringen, Germany).
Staining: Coomassie brilliant blue G-250
Temperature: 37 degreesC
TumorCellularity: 5-10% tumor surface
